L348: CONSORT 2010 checklist of information to include when reporting a randomised trial*
L349: | Section/Topic | Item No | Checklist item | Reported on page No |
L350: | --- | --- | --- | --- |
L351: | Title and abstract | Title and abstract | Title and abstract | Title and abstract |
L352: |  | 1a | Identification as a randomised trial in the title | 1 |
L353: |  | 1b | Structured summary of trial design, methods, results, and conclusions (for specific guidance see CONSORT for abstracts) | 3 |
L354: | Introduction | Introduction | Introduction | Introduction |
L355: | Background and objectives | 2a | Scientific background and explanation of rationale | 4 |
L356: | Background and objectives | 2b | Specific objectives or hypotheses | 4 |
L357: | Methods | Methods | Methods | Methods |
L358: | Trial design | 3a | Description of trial design (such as parallel, factorial) including allocation ratio | 5 |
L359: | Trial design | 3b | Important changes to methods after trial commencement (such as eligibility criteria), with reasons | N/A |
L360: | Participants | 4a | Eligibility criteria for participants | 6 |
L361: | Participants | 4b | Settings and locations where the data were collected | 5 |
L362: | Interventions | 5 | The interventions for each group with sufficient details to allow replication, including how and when they were actually administered | 6-7 |
L363: | Outcomes | 6a | Completely defined pre-specified primary and secondary outcome measures, including how and when they were assessed | 7-8 |
L364: | Outcomes | 6b | Any changes to trial outcomes after the trial commenced, with reasons | N/A |
L365: | Sample size | 7a | How sample size was determined | 5 |
L366: | Sample size | 7b | When applicable, explanation of any interim analyses and stopping guidelines | N/A |
L367: | Randomisation: |  |  |  |
L368: | Sequence generation | 8a | Method used to generate the random allocation sequence | 6 |
L369: | Sequence generation | 8b | Type of randomisation; details of any restriction (such as blocking and block size) | 6 |
L370: | Allocation concealment mechanism | 9 | Mechanism used to implement the random allocation sequence (such as sequentially numbered containers), describing any steps taken to conceal the sequence until interventions were assigned | 6 |
L371: | Implementation | 10 | Who generated the random allocation sequence, who enrolled participants, and who assigned participants to interventions | 6 |
L372: | Blinding | 11a | If done, who was blinded after assignment to interventions (for example, participants, care providers, those assessing outcomes) and how | 6 |
L373: | Blinding | 11b | If relevant, description of the similarity of interventions | N/A |
L374: | Statistical methods | 12a | Statistical methods used to compare groups for primary and secondary outcomes | 8-9 |
L375: | Statistical methods | 12b | Methods for additional analyses, such as subgroup analyses and adjusted analyses | 8-9 |
L376: | Results | Results | Results | Results |
L377: | Participant flow (a diagram is strongly recommended) | 13a | For each group, the numbers of participants who were randomly assigned, received intended treatment, and were analysed for the primary outcome | 9 |
L378: | Participant flow (a diagram is strongly recommended) | 13b | For each group, losses and exclusions after randomisation, together with reasons | N/A |
L379: | Recruitment | 14a | Dates defining the periods of recruitment and follow-up | 9 |
L380: | Recruitment | 14b | Why the trial ended or was stopped | N/A |
L381: | Baseline data | 15 | A table showing baseline demographic and clinical characteristics for each group | 16 |
L382: | Numbers analysed | 16 | For each group, number of participants (denominator) included in each analysis and whether the analysis was by original assigned groups | 9 |
L383: | Outcomes and estimation | 17a | For each primary and secondary outcome, results for each group, and the estimated effect size and its precision (such as 95% confidence interval) | 9 |
L384: | Outcomes and estimation | 17b | For binary outcomes, presentation of both absolute and relative effect sizes is recommended | N/A |
L385: | Ancillary analyses | 18 | Results of any other analyses performed, including subgroup analyses and adjusted analyses, distinguishing pre-specified from exploratory | N/A |
L386: | Harms | 19 | All important harms or unintended effects in each group (for specific guidance see CONSORT for harms) | N/A |
L387: | Discussion | Discussion | Discussion | Discussion |
L388: | Limitations | 20 | Trial limitations, addressing sources of potential bias, imprecision, and, if relevant, multiplicity of analyses | 10-11 |
L389: | Generalisability | 21 | Generalisability (external validity, applicability) of the trial findings | 10-11 |
L390: | Interpretation | 22 | Interpretation consistent with results, balancing benefits and harms, and considering other relevant evidence | 10-11 |
L391: | Other information | Other information | Other information |  |
L392: | Registration | 23 | Registration number and name of trial registry | 5 |
L393: | Protocol | 24 | Where the full trial protocol can be accessed, if available | N/A |
L394: | Funding | 25 | Sources of funding and other support (such as supply of drugs), role of funders | N/A |
L395: Citation: Schulz KF, Altman DG, Moher D, for the CONSORT Group. CONSORT 2010 Statement: updated guidelines for reporting parallel group randomised trials. BMC Medicine. 2010;8:18.
